                    insight_closed:         `Gap closed: you turned a stalled deck into execution — a credible trajectory to ≥70% backed by real buy-in and a 2027-milestone plan. You removed the barriers (incentives, capability, sequencing) instead of re-writing the strategy, exactly as Thomas prescribes.`,
                    insight_optics:         `Optics, not execution: the headline moved, but buy-in and the 2027 sustainability KPIs lagged badly. You leaned on the flagship launch and a paper number — the trajectory that collapses when the board looks past the launch event.`,
                    insight_thin:           `You moved the execution number, but the foundations are thin. Without aligned incentives, real ownership and co-created suppliers, the 2027 milestones are fragile and likely to slip.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the ≥70% execution trajectory. The loan steps up 75 bps (≈€2.1M/yr) and the two retail customers (22% of revenue) can delist. Re-examine the barriers you left in place — most likely the incentives and the sequencing.`,
                    insight_shelved:        `Near-zero execution at the 18-month review: the board has shelved Lumière 2030, triggering the loan penalty and the retail delisting risk together. The deck was never the problem — the barriers were, and they stayed in place.`,
                    insight_milestone_risk: `Sustainability KPIs Met is low — the 2027 customer and loan milestones are at risk. Foundations, capability and co-created suppliers are what make those milestones reachable; without them the covenant steps up.`,
                    insight_lowbuyin:       `Stakeholder buy-in stayed low: staff, suppliers and customers aren't behind the change. Co-creation and aligned incentives build buy-in; mandates and compliance letters erode it.`,
                    insight_lasts:          `This is execution that lasts: execution rate, buy-in and the 2027 sustainability KPIs moving together, owned per initiative and tracked at quarterly checkpoints. The strategy is finally being delivered, not just displayed.`,

                    hint_optics:            `You're leaning on optics — the flagship launch and a headline number. Fund the foundations and align the incentives, or the 2027 milestones won't actually land.`,
                    hint_milestone:         `Sustainability KPIs Met is dangerously low. Build capability, co-create with suppliers and customers, and commit to both 2027 milestones — or the loan steps up and the retailers can delist.`,
                    hint_buyin:             `Buy-in is very low — 38% already call it greenwash. Reconsider stakeholder engagement and incentives; co-creation and aligned rewards move people where mandates don't.`,
                    hint_behind:            `You're behind the ≥70% execution trajectory with little time left. Concentrate on the highest-leverage barriers — incentives and foundations-first sequencing.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — execution, buy-in and sustainability KPIs all healthy. Now lock in named owners and quarterly checkpoints so it survives past the launch.`,

